<title>USA: Bausch &amp; Lomb Q1 shr $0.06 after charge.</title>
<headline>Bausch &amp; Lomb Q1 shr $0.06 after charge.</headline>
<dateline>ROCHESTER, N.Y. 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>BAUSCH &amp; LOMB</p>
<p>							 Three Months Ended</p>
<p> Dollar Amounts in Millions		 Mar 29,	 Mar 30,</p>
<p> Except Per Share Data			   1997	    1996</p>
<p>Net Sales</p>
<p>  Vision Care				    $201.4	  $197.6</p>
<p>  Eyewear					   121.4	   137.4</p>
<p>  Pharmaceuticals				  49.0	    48.5</p>
<p>  Healthcare (A)				   79.4	    85.8</p>
<p> Total						451.2	   469.3</p>
<p>Costs and Expenses</p>
<p>  Cost of products sold			 227.2	   207.9</p>
<p>  Selling, administrative and general     181.0	   197.3</p>
<p>  Research and development		     15.6	    17.8</p>
<p>  Restructuring charges (B)		    12.8		--</p>
<p> Total						436.6	   423.0</p>
<p> Operating Earnings				14.6	    46.3</p>
<p>Other (Income) Expense</p>
<p>  Interest and investment income	   (10.0)	   (9.7)</p>
<p>  Interest expense				 13.6	    12.3</p>
<p>  (Gain) loss from foreign currency	 (1.2)		--</p>
<p> Total						  2.4	     2.6</p>
<p>Earnings Before Income Taxes</p>
<p>  and Minority Interest			  12.2	    43.7</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes		     4.3	    16.5</p>
<p> Earnings Before Minority Interest	    7.9	    27.2</p>
<p> Minority interest in subsidiaries	    4.6	     4.7</p>
<p> Net Earnings (C)				   3.3	    22.5</p>
<p> Net Earnings Per Common Share		 0.06	    0.39</p>
<p>Average Common Shares</p>
<p>  Outstanding (000s) (D)		     55,615	  57,108</p>
<p>(A)  1996 sales included $14.9 in first quarter revenues from the divested oral care and dental implant businesses.</p>
<p>(B)  Restructuring charges reduced first quarter 1997 net earnings by $7.7, or $0.14 per share.</p>
<p>(C)  Includes a provision of $6.8, or $0.12 per share after taxes for the expected cost of discontinuing certain product lines and writing off other investments in the eyewear segment.</p>
<p>(D)  Actual outstanding shares at 03/29/97 were 55,527.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
